_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in v4.6.beta1.official [d743736f8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta1 - cpe:/o:nixos:nixos:26.05 #1-NixOS SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon Nov 24 09:37:52 UTC 2025 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon 840M Graphics (RADV GFX1152) - AMD Ryzen AI 5 340 w/ Radeon 840M (12 threads) - 14.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen setting `MouseMode` to `MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED` the mouse should not be able to move outside of the embedded game window. While `MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED` correctly hides the mouse, it does not confine it to the embedded game window and dragging too far in any direction will move the mouse outside of it.\n\nThis was tested using the Niri compositor\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create godot project with a node with the following script\n```gdscript\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventMouseButton:\n\t\tDisplayServer.mouse_set_mode(DisplayServer.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)\n```\n- Run the project and click on the embedded game window\n- The mouse should now be hidden\n- drag the mouse in any direction for a while\n- the mouse will escape the embedded game window\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[embeddingexample.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24171735/embeddingexample.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u